import re
import unicodedata

def slugify(text):
    """Convert text to lowercase, remove accents, replace non-alphanumerics with a hyphen, and trim consecutive hyphens."""
    text = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', text).encode('ASCII', 'ignore').decode('utf-8')
    text = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9]+', '-', text)
    text = re.sub(r'-+', '-', text).strip('-')
    return text.lower()
```

This function first normalizes the Unicode string to decompose accented characters, then encodes it to ASCII while ignoring non-ASCII characters. Next, it replaces all non-alphanumeric characters with hyphens and then replaces consecutive hyphens with a single hyphen, before finally converting the string to lowercase. The function does not alter the existing tests in `test_textutil.py`.
